1
00:00:00,039 --> 00:00:04,630
Open the saved community support status
exercise and check its incident reference.

2
00:00:04,969 --> 00:00:09,289
Its badge reads Planned, and its finance
mode is Operational only.

3
00:00:09,630 --> 00:00:13,069
This separate fictional deployment has no
rostered resources,

4
00:00:13,189 --> 00:00:14,970
time reports or expenses.

5
00:00:15,310 --> 00:00:19,610
Keeping it separate makes each status
result easy to verify without changing

6
00:00:19,610 --> 00:00:21,049
the earlier training deployment.

7
00:00:21,430 --> 00:00:25,479
The badge on the left shows the stored
operational state; the dropdown in

8
00:00:25,479 --> 00:00:28,020
Summary prepares a possible next change.

9
00:00:28,199 --> 00:00:32,159
In Summary, choose Standby and select
Change status.

10
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:34,199
Confirm the change when prompted.

11
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:38,229
Before saving, the dropdown can say
Standby while the deployment

12
00:00:38,229 --> 00:00:39,739
badge still says Planned.

13
00:00:40,149 --> 00:00:44,139
After the page returns, verify Saved and
the Standby badge.

14
00:00:44,459 --> 00:00:48,119
This difference is important when a
supervisor checks whether an assignment is

15
00:00:48,119 --> 00:00:50,819
ready or merely has an unsaved selection.

16
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:55,100
Use the saved badge as the readback of the
operation you just performed.

17
00:00:55,350 --> 00:01:00,560
For the next stage, choose Active in the
same dropdown and select Change status.

18
00:01:00,939 --> 00:01:04,410
Confirm the intended transition, then read
the returned badge.

19
00:01:04,719 --> 00:01:06,259
It now says Active.

20
00:01:06,559 --> 00:01:11,030
The dropdown may already display the next
available choice after a save, so read

21
00:01:11,030 --> 00:01:12,890
it separately from the current badge.

22
00:01:13,239 --> 00:01:17,839
This exercise changes the deployment’s
operational stage; it does not dispatch a

23
00:01:17,839 --> 00:01:22,849
call or automatically demonstrate changes
to individual unit or personnel statuses.

24
00:01:23,019 --> 00:01:26,880
When the fictional assignment is winding
down, choose Demobilizing

25
00:01:27,030 --> 00:01:28,849
and select Change status.

26
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:32,480
Confirm it and verify the saved
Demobilizing badge.

27
00:01:32,770 --> 00:01:36,600
The same page retains the deployment
reference, window and notes.

28
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:39,699
Those details help you keep the status
change attached

29
00:01:39,699 --> 00:01:40,939
to the intended assignment.

30
00:01:41,390 --> 00:01:45,240
Time-report submission, independent
approval and equipment handover are

31
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:48,820
separate operations demonstrated in the
other deployment lessons;

32
00:01:49,210 --> 00:01:52,789
a status label does not establish that
those tasks were completed.

33
00:01:53,019 --> 00:01:57,590
Choose Completed and select Change status
for this empty training exercise.

34
00:01:57,970 --> 00:02:01,630
Confirm the transition and verify the
returned Completed badge.

35
00:02:01,980 --> 00:02:05,800
Compare that badge with the earlier
prepared dropdown so you can distinguish

36
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,640
selection from a saved result.

37
00:02:08,069 --> 00:02:11,419
In this completed view, the next-status
dropdown and Change

38
00:02:11,419 --> 00:02:13,470
status button are no longer offered.

39
00:02:13,839 --> 00:02:18,339
The Summary still shows zero resources,
time reports, personnel hours and

40
00:02:18,339 --> 00:02:20,630
expenses for this separate exercise.

41
00:02:20,770 --> 00:02:22,139
Return to Deployments.

42
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:26,319
The current list no longer includes the
completed status exercise.

43
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:28,029
Select Show all.

44
00:02:28,470 --> 00:02:31,990
The completed exercise now appears with
its Completed badge and

45
00:02:32,030 --> 00:02:34,009
Operational only finance mode.

46
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:38,529
The other active and demobilizing training
deployments remain separate rows.

47
00:02:38,970 --> 00:02:42,490
Use this view when you need retained
history rather than assuming that

48
00:02:42,490 --> 00:02:46,220
an assignment disappeared or was deleted
when it left the current list.

49
00:02:46,399 --> 00:02:49,250
Open the completed exercise from the
retained list.

50
00:02:49,659 --> 00:02:54,349
The fully loaded detail page still shows
Completed, the same incident reference,

51
00:02:54,519 --> 00:02:57,019
the window, contact and training notes.

52
00:02:57,380 --> 00:02:59,259
Operational only is retained.

53
00:02:59,820 --> 00:03:03,340
Reopening provides another check that the
result persisted beyond

54
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:04,809
the page on which you changed it.

55
00:03:05,219 --> 00:03:08,299
This demonstration follows the forward
status sequence that was

56
00:03:08,410 --> 00:03:12,110
actually available and saved; it does not
demonstrate a backward

57
00:03:12,110 --> 00:03:13,959
transition or a cancellation.

58
00:03:14,189 --> 00:03:18,319
Use deployment stages to keep assignments
understandable for your own department.

59
00:03:18,810 --> 00:03:22,500
Community paramedicine and mental health
teams can track a temporary

60
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:26,510
support assignment; search-and-rescue and
security departments can track

61
00:03:26,510 --> 00:03:30,780
an operation; wildland contractors and
industrial emergency teams

62
00:03:30,780 --> 00:03:32,149
can track a crew deployment.

63
00:03:32,639 --> 00:03:36,090
Fire and E M S organizations can use the
same controls.

64
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:41,289
Check the intended assignment, select its
next stage, save, and verify

65
00:03:41,289 --> 00:03:42,910
the badge and retained history.

66
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:47,250
Review time, equipment and finance through
their separate workflows.

